  Cure sickness at 0% failure will always work in one move, if you're
not confused and if you have the mana.  Remember, the AoY can triple
mana cost of spells.  I think it averages to twice as much mana usage if
you cast a spell while carrying the Amulet of Yendor.

  (Being stunned does not directly affect spell casting.  It will cause
some randomness with the direction given for directional spells, even if
you give yourself as the direction.  Since cure sickness is not a
directional, being stunned won't interfere with this at all.  This
explanation is given because Pestilence can stun you as well as sicken
you.)

  Blessed unihorn will save mana and should be good enough against
Pestilence, if you're patient and careful.  (Still better to kill
Pestilence from a distance, either yourself or by wearing a ring of
conflict.)  

  I relied on an uncursed unicorn horn many times against Pestilence in
my last game on NAO.  I never died from Illness, although there were a
few times I made absolutely sure I was wearing an amulet of Life Saving.


  Oh, yeah, carry about 20 k-rations into the Endgame.  One turn to eat,
plenty of nutrition.  Get Satiated (but no more) before entering the
Astral Plane, or at least before facing Famine.






